prior empty snapshots. Keep the correction local to settlement or declaration validation; do not introduce a second handler execution or a source-history scan. The Lending diagnostic preserves its original expected result and is not a claimed fix.\n\nValidation: I stable-copied the exact finite map (sha256 42085ddf5a632f0fc5b3300453779d6dd47143cba6e21ad72b1505d681d3ffa1) and its 106 owned regular files, and checked all 36 historical Git snapshots against Git. The listed dependency audit's 106 versions and 13 owned workspace links match the unchanged lock 3546b5384c9245fb646c4f7c22cabde0f4351b05dfcec704d1bdeb170666361a; zero installs are recorded, without a package-integrity claim or access to private dependency trees. Both focused controls fail at their intended assertions; the earlier suppression control predates later time/refused-pair tests and is not represented as a reconstructed later run. My independent Page regeneration is byte-exact: 822777 bytes, sha256 c156437ae513e6e66c76f423eccdcb0a1cbd8e49549ab3c4679c4cecc92d5c6d, with its 237-input graph excluding Wrangler/unenv and external first-party sources. Scratch dependencies were linked without installation. An initial tsx CLI invocation was sandbox-refused at IPC creation; node --import tsx completed both independent probes.\n\nThe original corrected gate at b44a8e255c36dd4654e07c6cc406d3633b5805ba/tree f2f45bc1d73a76e06c91557fbf612c605b02e8d5 completed in the original PTY 59168/terminal 4f4b19, exit 0: 387 Vitest files/1874 cases passed, one file/3 cases skipped, Node 31 and Counter 55 passed. The review candidate differs only in the primary note. Outer cost was 481.25 elapsed/676.04 CPU seconds on shared warm arm64 macOS 27.0.1, concurrent G1 work, starting load 1.24/2.43/2.49; this is not exclusive CPU, heap or total edit cost. The first gate at 8c117af37df12167793f52676b35195254cd2885/tree 33dd4cd1b9cc7b5301a4514584cbbbdd31830882 exited 1 with stale Page output and a Lending current-versus-behind mismatch